{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009265-clever-use-of-sympathy","id":1009265,"title":"Clever use of Sympathy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-28T03:54:34-08:00","id":1009265,"title":"Clever use of Sympathy","content":"So, you're a mage with a decent bit of Time and a bit more of Space and you come to find out that a good friend of yours is going to be targeted sympathetically (Spacially). You decide that that just won't do, so you cast borrow threads to capture that sympathetic connection whereupon you build yourself a mighty ward. Your Obrimos friend that has a touch of Fate says you have about a 60% chance of survival, but your skill with Time tells you that you'll be dead in 31 hours. You cancel the borrow threads spell and take some time to think. You then come up with a clever plan. You grab a stray cat, cast borrow threads to once again take the sympathetic connection upon yourself after which you cast borrow threads again and give that sympathetic connection to the cat. Would this work? If so, could you give the sympathetic connection to say, a tree or perhaps a rock?<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know that you could possibly do a similar thing with the spell Perfect Sympathy, but that still leaves you with a clash of wills which I'm trying to avoid. You get that same clash via ward).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:13:48-08:00","id":1009272,"title":"","content":"But the Yantra used for sympathetic targeting would be invalid since it's representational of the friend and not the Time/Space mage. Unless the Mage casting the spell double checks the target they'd just cast it and know it failed for unknown reasons.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's possible to chain cast Borrow Threads to transfer a connection two steps, but there is a Reach that allows you to transfer a connection between two subjects of the spell. Any object is a valid subject for Borrow Threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:17:20-08:00","id":1009274,"title":"","content":"I don't understand what you mean by trying to avoid a Clash from Perfect Sympathy because you get a Clash from Ward...?<br /> <br /> But for the Borrow Threads + Ward method, I see why not. It'd be hillarious watching a tree suddenly burst into splinters.<br /> <br /> However, Borrow Threads would need to include both the friend and his attacker with increased Scale, because the spell targets sympathetic links between the mage herself and her subject at default Scale. That's the part I find tricky - who is trying to attack the friend? Is it someone who already has a link to him? If so, can you get both of them within your range and cast a spell on both of them without the attacker knowing?<br /> Then again, the attacker might be using Borrow Threads himself to attack the friend. If so, then which of the friend's links were borrowed? Is there a practical way to find out, considering a person is often linked to dozens of people and objects?<br /> <br /> Hmm... maybe using Veil Sympathy's Reach option to shut down all the friend's links is more useful? I don't recall that effect triggering a Clash at all, so it'd be easier on the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:42:14-08:00","id":1009280,"title":"","content":"You don't need all parts of a sympathetic connection present or include into scale for borrow threads. The scale factor is if you want to transfer or copy connections between more subjects at the same time. With a potency of 3, a scale of 3 subjects and a reach for direct transfer a mage could change 3 sympathetic connections freely between his retainer, his dog and himself. For example give 1 connection from himself to each his dog and his retainer and one from the retainer to the dog.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a> if your mage knows which connection the attacker will use, you can easily transfer that one to any object and the spell will fail, cause the attacker cannot target the object with the same sympathetic yantra. If you do this for a while it might result in other problems though. If you transfer the connection between the partner of the mage and the mage himself e.g., the partner might get weirdly affectionate about that one particular tree in the forest or the connection might start to wither due to negligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:55:55-08:00","id":1009282,"title":"","content":"A withered connection isn't a problem given the sympathetic connection is to bodily fluids recently expelled. Ah, veil sympathy, I forgot about that one. Definitely stuff to think about. I'll be back after sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T06:34:25-08:00","id":1009301,"title":"","content":"Veil Sympathy could work, if you're not worried about winning that Clash of Wills. I'd go with a Fraying/Unravelling spell (Cut Threads, if you got an Adept handy, or something improvised and probably not Lasting if all you have is a Disciple) aimed directly at the connections themselves - don't need to hide something that's not there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:47:43-08:00","id":1009517,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the mage isn't an adept. I thought of that one. Also, the contest of wills would be a close one. That's why I wanted to bypass it altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}